<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Serbian Progressive Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2008</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as SNS</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Serbian Progressive Party is a Serbian political party founded in 2008 by Tomislav Nikolić and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleksandar-vucic">Aleksandar Vučić</a>, who broke away from the nationalist Serbian Radical Party. It has led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>'s governments since 2012. The party combines a stated goal of joining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a> with close relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/serbian-progressive-party.jpg" alt="Serbian Progressive Party" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ThecentreCZ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Serbian_Progressive_Party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
